			<item>
				<title>Find the memory consumption of a Python Object</title>
				<link>https://jadi.space/blog/find-the-memory-consumption-of-a-python-object/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 24 Oct 2024 06:55:36 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://jadi.space/blog/find-the-memory-consumption-of-a-python-object/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Here is the snippet I use. Its not perfect but does the job.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;import sys&#xA;from types import ModuleType, FunctionType&#xA;from gc import get_referents&#xA;&#xA;# Custom objects know their class.&#xA;# Function objects seem to know way too much, including modules.&#xA;# Exclude modules as well.&#xA;BLACKLIST = type, ModuleType, FunctionType&#xA;&#xA;def getsize(obj):&#xA;    &amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;sum size of object &amp;amp; members.&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&#xA;    if isinstance(obj, BLACKLIST):&#xA;        raise TypeError(&amp;#39;getsize() does not take argument of type: &amp;#39;+ str(type(obj)))&#xA;    seen_ids = set()&#xA;    size = 0&#xA;    objects = [obj]&#xA;    while objects:&#xA;        need_referents = []&#xA;        for obj in objects:&#xA;            if not isinstance(obj, BLACKLIST) and id(obj) not in seen_ids:&#xA;                seen_ids.add(id(obj))&#xA;                size += sys.getsizeof(obj)&#xA;                need_referents.append(obj)&#xA;        objects = get_referents(*need_referents)&#xA;    return size&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a&#xA;  href=&#34;https://medium.com/@jadi/find-the-memory-consumption-of-a-python-object-69a803b144a8&#34;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;    class=&#34;link--external&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer&#34;&#xA;  &#xA;&gt;Medium&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>How to use SOAP/WSDL APIs using SoapUI &amp; Python Zeep</title>
				<link>https://jadi.space/blog/how-to-use-soap-wsdl-apis-using-soapui-python-zeep/</link>
				<pubDate>Sat, 01 Jul 2023 13:20:57 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://jadi.space/blog/how-to-use-soap-wsdl-apis-using-soapui-python-zeep/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;In our Agile / Mobile / “moderm” and fron/back life, we see lots of REST APIs. Using REST is straight forward if you know your HTTP, GET, Post, …&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;&#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;      &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;      &#xA;    &#xA;      &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;      &#xA;    &#xA;      &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;      &#xA;    &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;picture&gt;&#xA;      &lt;source&#xA;        type=&#34;image/webp&#34;&#xA;        srcset=&#34;https://jadi.space/blog/how-to-use-soap-wsdl-apis-using-soapui-python-zeep/img-01_hu_913a14fe5ff510ce.webp 300w,/blog/how-to-use-soap-wsdl-apis-using-soapui-python-zeep/img-01_hu_838221cc3f21f4d0.webp 500w,/blog/how-to-use-soap-wsdl-apis-using-soapui-python-zeep/img-01_hu_cc32819de75f2235.webp 700w&#34;&#xA;        sizes=&#34;(max-width: 499px) 300px,(max-width: 699px) 500px,700px&#34;&#xA;      /&gt;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xA;        src=&#34;https://jadi.space/blog/how-to-use-soap-wsdl-apis-using-soapui-python-zeep/img-01.png&#34;&#xA;        srcset=&#34;https://jadi.space/blog/how-to-use-soap-wsdl-apis-using-soapui-python-zeep/img-01_hu_1cc802aa84f38bfe.png 300w,/blog/how-to-use-soap-wsdl-apis-using-soapui-python-zeep/img-01_hu_45262d90072175e5.png 500w,/blog/how-to-use-soap-wsdl-apis-using-soapui-python-zeep/img-01_hu_cacd66e038c101a3.png 700w&#34;&#xA;        sizes=&#34;(max-width: 499px) 300px,(max-width: 699px) 500px,700px&#34;&#xA;        alt=&#34;How to use SOAP/WSDL APIs using SoapUI &amp;amp; Python Zeep&#34;&#xA;        &#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;        width=&#34;1024&#34;&#xA;        height=&#34;1024&#34;&#xA;      /&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/picture&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But on the enterprise level, you will start seein SOAP and WSDL based APIs which look more confusing. Why? Because they are designed machines in mind and sometimes WSDL file is seen as the &lt;em&gt;documentation&lt;/em&gt; and you wont get a human readable doc!&lt;/p&gt;</description>
